+# API reference
+
+Generated from the API endpoint metadata after Batch 3. The accompanying `openapi.json` describes request/response schemas and can be imported into an API client. Its server URL is relative (`/`); set your actual HTTPS base URL in that client. Retrieve the live specification at `/openapi/v1.json` with a stakeholder bearer token. No Swagger UI website is installed.
+
+Read `usage-guide.md` for business rules, examples, permissions, retry behavior, and workflow order. All paths below are relative to the API base address. Role checks also enforce branch assignments and active-account/session checks. Sellers only see their own sale invoices.
+
+Success codes below come from endpoint metadata. Common failures include 400 validation, 401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 404 missing/inaccessible, 409 business/concurrency conflict, 429 rate limit, and 500/503 server/dependency errors. See the usage guide for handling; not every failure applies to every route.
+
+## POST /api/auth/confirm-email
